## 🖥️ Compute environment

This project targets **PyTorch**{% if compute_backend == 'cuda' %} on **NVIDIA GPUs**{% endif %}:

- **Python** {{ python_version }}+
- **PyTorch** `{{ torch_version }}` / **torchvision** `{{ torchvision_version }}`
- **Compute backend**: {% if compute_backend == 'cuda' %}CUDA **{{ cuda_version }}** — wheels come from the dedicated PyTorch index (`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu{{ cuda_version | replace('.', '') }}`){% else %}CPU — wheels come from the CPU PyTorch index (`https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu`){% endif %} configured in [`pyproject.toml`](./pyproject.toml); `uv sync` installs them.

### Switching the compute backend

The backend is the `[[tool.uv.index]]` named `pytorch` in `pyproject.toml`
(`cu126` / `cu128` / `cu130`, or `.../whl/cpu`). After changing it,
re-resolve with `uv lock && uv sync` — or re-run
`copier update --UNSAFE --vcs-ref pytorch` and re-answer
`compute_backend` / `cuda_version`.

